I chose the **ai** variant because Langfuse is an open-source (MIT) platform for teams building with LLMs, covering tracing, evaluations and prompt management. The CV passes the checker on one page, and the mail is written. **Flags:** Langfuse stores traces in ClickHouse and other data in PostgreSQL, and neither is in facts.yaml, so the CV shows MongoDB/MySQL/Redis instead; the same goes for OpenTelemetry, where the CV shows the Prometheus/Loki work; Hsan has no LLM-as-a-judge evaluation experience, so the CV points to the KubeMind comparison of three model providers; Langfuse joined ClickHouse in January 2026, its jobs are listed on the ClickHouse careers site, and European roles are remote-first with regular visits to Berlin.
